   "lines": [
    "Early in morning went",
    "out to Chestnut Hill",
    "and, oh! how delighted",
    "I was to clasp my",
    "beloved darling again",
    "in my arms! She has",
    "received about 250",
    "presents.",
    "In the afternoon",
    "I went out with",
    "dear old Cotta[?] Peabody",
    "(whom I am very",
    "fond of) to the",
    "Peabodys house at",
    "Kernwood, Salem. It is",
    "a superb place; both",
    "grounds and house",
    "being strikingly handsome.",
    "Besides, I like the whole",
    "household very much;",
    "they are all so well read",
    "and intelligent — and",
    "the boys such stalwart,",
    "manly fellows"
   ],
